{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04YX", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-properties-lemma-monomorphism}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-second-diagonal}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-properties-diagonal-representable}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:582771791ced6804dcb483a6b1c44c45b973b776a462301fccb3fbedaa5681b1", "source_text": "Recall from Properties of Stacks, Lemma\n<REF_0001>\nthat a morphism of algebraic stacks is a monomorphism\nif and only if its diagonal is an isomorphism of stacks.\nThus Lemma <REF_0002>\ncan be rephrased as saying that a morphism is\nrepresentable by algebraic spaces if the diagonal\nis a monomorphism. In particular, it shows that condition\n(3) of Lemma <REF_0003>\nis actually an if and only if, i.e., a morphism of algebraic stacks\nis representable by algebraic spaces if and only if\nits diagonal is a monomorphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2b4c0f32578cd22583d329ff32952ee2ed32f04a80312556d5e41206edb19a2a", "unit_id": "tag:0AHJ:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04YX", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Delta_{f, 1}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Leftrightarrow$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Delta_{f, 2}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Leftrightarrow$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Delta_{f, 2}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Leftrightarrow$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Delta_{f, 2}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\Delta_{f, 1}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\Leftrightarrow$", "MATH_0011": "$\\Delta_{f, 2}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\Leftrightarrow$", "MATH_0013": "$\\Delta_{f, 2}$", "MATH_0014": "$\\Delta_{f, 1}$", "MATH_0015": "$\\Leftrightarrow$", "MATH_0016": "$\\Delta_{f, 2}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-first-diagonal-separated-second-diagonal-closed}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:661b966450cf1dd67ca4f320532f7a875783d304f4bde9afe2e07dd55ffbf721", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ac5bb7542ea91c88b86e227b8f00461cb34e97e55ef142b6a9a7c5bf8193be44", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks.\nThen\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> separated <MATH_0003>\n<MATH_0004> closed immersion <MATH_0005>\n<MATH_0006> proper <MATH_0007>\n<MATH_0008> universally closed,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0009> quasi-separated <MATH_0010>\n<MATH_0011> finite type <MATH_0012> <MATH_0013> quasi-compact,\nand\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0014> locally separated <MATH_0015>\n<MATH_0016> immersion.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:62fc05836a3d3c7a56cfda960f726763c99484b1b504b726319342267ec6f2de", "unit_id": "tag:04YZ:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04YX", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Delta_{f, 1}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-representable-separated-diagonal-closed}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-representable-quasi-separated-diagonal-quasi-compact}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-representable-locally-separated-diagonal-immersion}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c6845be1f3e4c524ccca25c94d7ad2c3a8a086633f848e8895a7e407be853ae4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:57bc4fee376ecb630f4a8a9a08bf20f1a9f647f69fbddb64244a195dc1649a4f", "source_text": "Follows from\nLemmas <REF_0001>,\n<REF_0002>, and\n<REF_0003>\napplied to <MATH_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:362f1bc2c36ba3a0af124f556a29596abcedda9c52f072c734799d9c4b309722", "unit_id": "tag:04YZ:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04YX", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:308d3b2e4452415397257f35b4561d751a23645c6e16c4f2f9eb5c16db7326e9", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe following lemma is kind of cute and it may suggest a generalization\nof these conditions to higher algebraic stacks.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bbbf1408affc03e782f36b3dbdba1954e9398f8cdb6a0c53e2f9dcbebe549c88", "unit_id": "tag:04YX:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04YX", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Delta_{f, 1}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Delta_{f, 2}$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Delta_{f, 1}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Delta_{f, 2}$", "MATH_0008": "$f$", "MATH_0009": "$\\Delta_{f, 1}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\Delta_{f, 2}$", "MATH_0011": "$f$", "MATH_0012": "$\\Delta_{f, 1}$", "MATH_0013": "$\\Delta_{f, 2}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-definition-separated}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a0bdeb64ea76de468beca403d611b78b3c84f3137aad9135a5432fbae162eec9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e783b7c9baa6a2c3dcba2fd0dabc817449a69fc62194d71430997066333cdf13", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks.\nThen\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is separated if and only if <MATH_0003> and <MATH_0004>\nare universally closed, and\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0005> is quasi-separated if and only if <MATH_0006> and <MATH_0007>\nare quasi-compact.\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0008> is quasi-DM if and only if <MATH_0009> and <MATH_0010>\nare locally quasi-finite.\n<STRUCT_0005> <MATH_0011> is DM if and only if <MATH_0012> and <MATH_0013>\nare unramified.\n<STRUCT_0006>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:aab70e9ed749819745f62f94d99e2db48db0853c3fad60240336dc475324e292", "unit_id": "tag:04Z0:statement"}
